KG42.register("rules-13b67f8e2069fd9be7e04bb7",{"id":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R007","paper":"33-retail_market_interoperability","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R007","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Consumer participation","process_stage":"participation","market_meaning":"Consumer players may participate without a numerical limit. Each load entity, including ES in charging mode, NRL and RLD, is treated as an independent consumer. Scope: Consumer players in the proposed H-MG retail market. A single H-MG may include a consumer player alongside a generator player. Scope: Consumer participation within a single H-MG in the general market formulation.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function participation.consumer under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["participation.consumer"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"participation","context_text":"Consumer participation within a single H-MG in the general market formulation. | Consumer players in the proposed H-MG retail market.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-e033"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Consumer players may participate without a numerical limit. Each load entity, including ES in charging mode, NRL and RLD, is treated as an independent consumer. Scope: Consumer players in the proposed H-MG retail market.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.consumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g02-e033"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"A single H-MG may include a consumer player alongside a generator player. Scope: Consumer participation within a single H-MG in the general market formulation.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.consumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E02","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p03-c2r1__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"2. H-MG concept","anchor_text":"ower Systems Research 157 (2018) 187–199 189 an building can be deﬁned perfectly as a microgrid with","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Each H-MG can have generation resources (controllable distributed energy resources (DER) and NDU), load (non-responsive load (NRL) and RLD), and ES devices. Every generation unit, DR during load reduction, and storage in discharging mode are classified as an individual generator, while each load entity (i.e. ES in charging mode, NRL, and RLD) is tagged as an independent consumer. In this framework, each player is trying to satisfy its own objective(s), i.e., generators try to maximize their profit while consumers look after minimizing their operation cost."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E04","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"3. The proposed retail market structure","anchor_text":"a single H-MG can have both generator and consumer as players in the market. This feature is preferr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Another feature of H-MGs in this study is that a single H-MG can have both generator and consumer as players in the market. This feature is preferred in this study to generalize market operation and formulation for every ownership situation, such as when tenants of the H-MG are not the owner of the building, generation and storage devices."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e033","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"7. Simulation results and discussions","anchor_text":"13) with MCEMS, is attempting to only minimize its operation cost. It is used as the base-case schem","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Please note that there is no limitation on the number of players, including generator, consumer, and retailer."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"No optimization or operational decision variable is in scope for this participation rule. The source statements define eligibility and player-role classification, not a decision quantity. The consumer dispatch/cost objective in Eq. (10) is outside R007's frozen node participation.consumer and belongs to clearing/pricing formalization.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed parameter, coefficient, or numerical input is defined by the frozen R007 participation statements. Player-count and load-entity role statements are qualitative/procedural and the source provides no R007-specific parameter value or algebraic eligibility formula."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"participation.consumer","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e033","quote":"Please note that there is no limitation on the number of players, including generator, consumer, and retailer."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E02","quote":"each load entity (i.e. ES in charging mode, NRL, and RLD) is tagged as an independent consumer."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E04","quote":"Another feature of H-MGs in this study is that a single H-MG can have both generator and consumer as players in the market."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"37d8ebd6db9b300f70a16a4196544cedad4c05867fe323437cd1a26d1e773a0c","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"Rule R007 governs consumer eligibility and role classification: consumer players may participate without a numerical limit, each load entity is treated as an independent consumer, and a single H-MG may contain both consumer and generator players. These are procedural/admission statements, not equations or optimization constraints. The source does contain consumer operation-cost mathematics in Eq. (10), but that formulation is part of clearing/pricing scope, while this frozen rule has only the node participation.consumer and no corresponding variable, parameter, or edge structure. B evidence remains unreviewed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","node_ids":["participation.consumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C001 states consumer eligibility, unrestricted player count, and load-entity role classification. It attaches to the frozen participation.consumer node; no frozen edge is required or available."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C002","node_ids":["participation.consumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C002 states that one H-MG may contain both consumer and generator players. It scopes consumer participation under the sole frozen participation.consumer node; no frozen edge is required or available."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
